  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Action Aid - Sexual &amp; Reproductive Rights</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Action Aid Liberia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Overall objective
Women, girls and groups exposed to stigma and discrimination across Liberia enjoy fundamental human rights as a result of the claims of a strengthened advocacy oriented civil society and evidence of quality responses from local government and the state.
Specific Objectives:
Objective 1: Women, girls and particularly discriminated groups have improved access to sexual and reproductive health and rights
Objective 2: Women and girls have increased protection from all forms of violence, abuse and exploitation through improved monitoring, risk assessment and prevention efforts.
Objective 3: Capacity of state and non-state actors at sub-national level in 6 counties are strengthened to integrate gender and human rights in the provision of services affecting vulnerable women, youth and girls
Objective 4: An inter-agency development forum developed to act with coordinated and enhanced capacity to influence gender and human rights in targeted policies and development plans at national level.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektet syftar till att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra skyddet och r&#xe4;ttigheterna f&#xf6;r     kvinnor, flickor och andra diskriminerade grupper i sex l&#xe4;n i         Liberia. Det tar upp fr&#xe5;gor som r&#xf6;r sexuell och reproduktiv h&#xe4;lsa och r&#xe4;ttigheter, inklusive kvinnlig k&#xf6;nsstympning och diskriminering av   sexuella minoriteter som bland annat HBT personer.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to enhance the protection and rights of women, girls and other groups facing discrimination in 45 communities in four      counties in Liberia. The project will address issues relating to      sexual and reproductive health and rights including female genital    multilation,and discrimination of sexual minorities, including        respect for the human rights of LGBTI.</narrative>
  </description>
